Title

    compmed -- Compliance adjusted causal mediation analysis

Syntax

        compmed outcome, mvar(mediator) dvar(receipt) rvar(rgroup) 
                 [cvars(varlist) method(method) vce(vcetype) breps(#) seed(#) 
                  FULLoutput] 

    outcome and mediator must be continuous, receipt and rgroup must be binary. 
    rgroup is coded 0 for the control group and 1 for the treatment group. 
    receipt is coded 0 for not having received treatment, and 1 for having 
    received treatment. If compliance is measured on a continuous scale, one 
    must create a binary compliance indicator. cvars should consist of 
    baseline mediator and outcome scores when available in the dataset.

    options                    Description
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------
    cvars(varlist)             baseline covariates to be included in the 
			         receipt, mediator, and outcome structural 
				 models.
    breps(#)                   specifies the number of bootstrap replications
			         to be performed; default is breps(1000)    
    seed(#)		       sets the random-number seed to #. If unspecified
				 the seed will be a random number between 1 and
				 1000.
    vce(vcetype)	       vcetype may be oim, robust, cluster clustervar, or
				 bootstrap
    method(method)             method may be ml or mlmv
    FULLoutput                 reports decomposition of effects into total, 
			         direct, and indirect
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description

    compmed implements a compliance-adjusted causal mediation analysis for 
    estimating the complier average causal effect (CACE) and its decomposition 
    into the complier average causal mediated effect (CACME) and the complier 
    average natural direct effect (CANDE). The command fits a structural equation 
    model (SEM) within a unified efficacy mechanism evaluation framework.

Options

    cvars(varlist) specifies any baseline covariates to be included as covariates
        in the receive, mediator, and outcome structural models.

    breps(#) specifies the number of bootstrap replications to be performed;
	default is breps(1000)    
    
    seed(#) sets the random-number seed to #. If unspecified the seed will be a 
	random number between 1 and 1000.

    vce(vcetype) specifies the technique used to obtain the variance-covariance 
        matrix of the estimates (VCE), which includes the reported standard 
        errors; default is vce(oim). 

    method(method) specifies the method used to obtain parameter estimates; 
        default is method(ml).

    FULLoutput reports the decomposition of effects into total, direct, and 
        indirect effects.


Example

    Use compmed to estimate the CACME, CANDE, and CACE (minimum specification)
        . compmed Y, mvar(M) dvar(D) rvar(R)

    Use compmed to estimate the CACME, CANDE, and CACE, adjusting for baseline
      mediator and outcome values (recommended approach)
        . compmed Y, mvar(M) dvar(D) rvar(R) cvars(Y0 M0) 

    Use compmed to estimate the CACME, CANDE, and CACE, adjusting for baseline
      mediator and outcome values and accounting for clustering by Therapist
        . compmed Y, mvar(M) dvar(D) rvar(R) cvars(Y0 M0) vce(cl Therapist)


References

    Chis Ster, A. (2026). "A unified approach to a statistical efficacy and
	mechanism evaluation in clinical trials." Under review. 

    Yamamoto, Teppei. 2013. 'Identification and Estimation of Causal Mediation Effects 
	with Treatment Noncompliance', Unpublished manuscript.

    Park, Soojin, and Esra Kürüm. 2020. 'A Two-Stage Joint Modeling Method for Causal 
	Mediation Analysis in the Presence of Treatment Noncompliance', Journal of 
	Causal Inference, 8: 131-49.

